{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumEMZpRWrMQsHYmH2mC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As far as I know, Cloudflare Workflows has no per-workflow \"max concurrent instances\" setting. The only concurrency limit is the account-level one, which depends on your plan. Check the current Workflows limits docs, since this may have changed.\n\nTo cap it yourself, put a gate in front of instance creation:\n\n- **Durable Object semaphore:** Keep a counter in a single Durable Object. Before calling `env.MY_WORKFLOW.create()`, ask the DO for a slot. If none is free, queue or reject the request. Have the workflow release its slot in a final step (wrapped in try/catch so failures also release it). Add a timeout or alarm to reclaim slots from instances that die without releasing.\n- **Queues:** Send creation requests through a Queue, and have the consumer start workflows only when the DO says there is capacity. Setting `max_concurrency` on the consumer only limits consumer invocations, not how many workflow instances are running, so it isn't a cap on its own."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2251,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2251},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2491737-501f-4e66-877a-f38f908bd131","uuid":"50bac5b1-7e8b-4f37-a917-14878b625f19","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:46:26.079Z","request_id":"req_011CfumEMKgxnJKM2ocHHrx9"}
